    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0356" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7442/18</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manchester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                        1925</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 21.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 823</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of September
                        15th<anchor n="1" xml:id="d216-f1"/> concerning the proposed reciprocal
                    agreement by an exchange of notes between the United States Government and His
                    Majesty’s Government for preventing interference by ships with
                    radiobroadcasting, I have the honour, under instructions from His Majesty’s
                    Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs, to inform you that the
                    Canadian Government desire to conclude with the United States Government a <pb
                        facs="0357" n="275" xml:id="pg275"/> reciprocal agreement in terms similar
                    to those proposed in my note No. 796 of September 8th.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Chilton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
